{
  "note": "RFC 4271 Section 9.1.2 requires excluding any BGP route whose NEXT_HOP is unresolvable or would become unresolvable if installed. Unit tests over real Loc-RIB and igpcost.ResolveProspective prove exclusion of an unresolved higher-LOCAL_PREF candidate, a lone unresolved candidate, self/mutual recursive loops, and direct/indirect prospective self-capture, while negative controls prove zero-cost reachable, valid recursive static, longer interior prefix inside NLRI, and same-prefix connected routes remain admissible. Four functional .ci tests verify current and prospective exclusion plus valid controls end-to-end into Linux kernel tables for both internal and forked bgp-rib placements.",
